WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.152
Let’s review what you can now do.

00:00:02.152 --> 00:00:09.862
You can create dictionaries, retrieve values safely, update records, loop through key-value pairs,

00:00:09.862 --> 00:00:17.416
and build frequency counts. You can use sets to remove duplicates, compare groups, and validate membership.

00:00:18.061 --> 00:00:22.988
These structures give us more realistic ways to organize data in Python.

00:00:22.988 --> 00:00:28.864
Next, we’ll use packages and object-oriented ideas to organize larger programs.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:34.507
In Module 6, we’ll focus on organizing larger Python programs.

00:00:34.507 --> 00:00:39.952
You’ll see how modules and packages help separate code into reusable files,

00:00:39.952 --> 00:00:46.822
and we’ll introduce object-oriented programming so related data and behavior can be organized together.

00:00:46.822 --> 00:00:51.853
This is an important step from small scripts toward maintainable applications.
